# Bash hooks / helper scripts must stay LF for Git Bash on Windows.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.gitattributes text eol=lf

# Why diary + agent-audit used to conflict: both `main` and a story branch
# append to the *same few files* after diverging from a common ancestor. Git's
# default merge then sees two independent edits touching the same region and
# often stops with a conflict even when both sides only *appended*.
#
# `merge=union` uses Git's union merge driver: the result is the union of
# lines from both parents — appropriate for append-only JSONL and for diary
# lines that are mostly independent additions. Keep appending; commit on the
# PR branch; merge to `main` without stripping.
# See: https://git-scm.com/docs/gitattributes#_built-in_merge_drivers
docs/diary/** merge=union
docs/agent-audit/agent-audit.jsonl merge=union
